### `validation` on a field is a CHECK constraint the database enforces for every writer. Each refusal
### is 422 `check` at the field to fix; each boundary value beside it is the control that makes the
### refusal the condition and not the field's type.

### An opening hour past the day's last
# @name OpensAt25
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [422]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/customers
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tenant_id": "{{tenantNorth}}", "name": "OpensAt25 Ltd", "tier": "standard", "service_opens_hour": 25 }

### Closing before opening — the closing hour's validation reads the opening hour of the same row
# @name ClosesBeforeOpens
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [422]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/customers
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tenant_id": "{{tenantNorth}}", "name": "ClosesBeforeOpens Ltd", "tier": "standard", "service_opens_hour": 18, "service_closes_hour": 8 }

### A sane window, 07-19 (control)
# @name SaneHours
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/customers
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tenant_id": "{{tenantNorth}}", "name": "SaneHours Ltd", "tier": "standard", "service_opens_hour": 7, "service_closes_hour": 19 }

### The edges of the window are admitted: 0 and 24 (control)
# @name EdgeHours
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/customers
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tenant_id": "{{tenantNorth}}", "name": "EdgeHours Ltd", "tier": "standard", "service_opens_hour": 0, "service_closes_hour": 24 }

### Priority 0 is outside 1..5
# @name PriorityZero
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [422]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tenant_id": "{{tenantNorth}}", "reference": "WO-3211", "title": "Integrity: WO-3211", "status": "new", "priority": 0, "access_code": "ACME-3211", "customer_id": "{{CustomerAcmeId}}", "region_id": "{{RegionNorthId}}" }

### A negative quote
# @name NegativeQuote
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [422]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tenant_id": "{{tenantNorth}}", "reference": "WO-3212", "title": "Integrity: WO-3212", "status": "new", "priority": 3, "access_code": "ACME-3212", "customer_id": "{{CustomerAcmeId}}", "region_id": "{{RegionNorthId}}", "quoted_price": -1.00 }

### Priority 5 and a zero quote are the boundaries, and pass (control)
# @name BoundaryValues
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tenant_id": "{{tenantNorth}}", "reference": "WO-3213", "title": "Integrity: WO-3213", "status": "new", "priority": 5, "access_code": "ACME-3213", "customer_id": "{{CustomerAcmeId}}", "region_id": "{{RegionNorthId}}", "quoted_price": 0.00 }
